# Firecracker jailer: attach container rootfs as a jail-owned device node.
#
# The identity repair bind-mounts /dev/dm-N onto the jail drive placeholder
# and then chowns that path so the non-root jailer can open it. Bind-mount
# plus chown rewrites the host device inode. udev then races the next
# container (init succeeded, app bind_mounts /dev/dm-N ENOENT).
#
# Kernel and guest image stay bind-mounted files. Host /dev/* block devices
# are recreated inside the jail with the same major:minor and jailer uid,
# so Firecracker can open them without mutating host /dev/dm-N.
diff --git a/src/runtime-rs/crates/hypervisor/src/firecracker/fc_api.rs b/src/runtime-rs/crates/hypervisor/src/firecracker/fc_api.rs
--- a/src/runtime-rs/crates/hypervisor/src/firecracker/fc_api.rs
+++ b/src/runtime-rs/crates/hypervisor/src/firecracker/fc_api.rs
@@ -20,9 +20,11 @@
